FMOD Engine for Debian

  * Package FMOD Engine
    - fmod-dev: metapackage with everything
    - fmod-doc: [doc]
  * Package FMOD Core API [api/core]
    - libfmod, libfmodl: [api/core/lib]
    - libfmod-dev: [api/core/inc]
    - libfmod-examples: [api/core/examples]
  * Package FMOD FSBank API [api/fsbank]
    - libfsbank, libfsbankl: [api/fsbank/lib]
    - libfsbank-dev: [api/fsbank/inc]
  * Package FMOD Studio API [api/studio]
    - libfmodstudio, libfmodstudiol: [api/studio/lib]
    - libfmodstudio-dev: [api/studio/inc]
    - libfmodstudio-examples: [api/studio/examples]
  * Package FMOD Engine tools [bin]
  * Exclude vendored Qt
    - remove RPATH $ORIGIN/lib
    - remove NEEDED libicu*.so.73
    - requires Qt 6.9, available in resolute or later
  * Exclude example media
    - EULA is very clear about no redistribution ever
    - It must be acquired directly from upstream
    - Providing the example code is still useful
  * Un-vendor libopus
    - NB: libfsbank dllopens plain libopus.so
    - Thus we have a dynamic dependency on libopus-dev
  * Keep vendored libfsbvorbis
    - Custom libvorbis used for libfsbank

Download the vendor tarball from <https://www.fmod.com/download#fmodengine>.
FMOD is non-free software; you must create an account and agree to their EULA.
No debian/watch is provided

To build:
  mk-origtargz ../fmodstudioapi20400linux.tar.gz
  tar -xf ../fmod_2.04.00.orig.tar.xz --strip-components=1
  debuild --lintian-opts -E --pedantic
